# scripts/ci-security-grep.allowlist — false-positive allowlist for the
# CI security grep step (see scripts/ci-security-grep.sh).
#
# Format: one entry per line, shaped `<path>:<substring-of-matched-line>`.
# Blank lines and lines beginning with `#` are ignored. Every allowlisted
# hit MUST carry a preceding comment explaining why it is safe.
#
# The 2026-07-28 SECURITY_AUDIT.md sweep found no os.system, no shell=True,
# no bare eval/exec, no pickle.loads, and no bare yaml.load in this tree.
# The file is intentionally empty of entries; downstream PRs add rows only
# with a documented justification.

# Grove v0.9 PR 12 (Loki finding m34): the regression test for
# scripts/ci-security-grep.sh pins that its PATTERN alternation matches
# the docstring's claimed pattern list. To do that it necessarily
# contains those pattern names verbatim inside its own docstring and
# assertions. Legitimate false positives — this is the witness for
# the sweep, not a shell invocation.
tests/test_ci_security_grep_docstring_matches_pattern.py:os.system(
tests/test_ci_security_grep_docstring_matches_pattern.py:os\.system\(
tests/test_ci_security_grep_docstring_matches_pattern.py:subprocess.Popen(...shell=True
